[00:16.00]costly a. 昂贵的；代价高的；损失大的；奢华的 示例 ① For makers of processed nosh, costly raw materials are a problem. ConAgra, General Mills, Kellogg's and Kraft recently raised prices for many of their wares. 对于食品制造商来说，昂贵的食品原料却不是好事。美国康尼格拉集团、通用磨坊食品公司和卡夫食品有限公司最近都提高了他们生产的许多商品的价格。（The Economist） ② The intricate and costly style of the lace ruff worn by the man in the portrait was characteristic of that period. 肖像画里男人穿戴的复杂又昂贵的花边状衣领是那个时代的特征。
[00:28.08]attendant n. 服务员；随从；伴随物；随之而来的结果‖a. 伴随的，随之而来的 示例 ① American claims that passengers will benefit from the change because the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) rules will force it to add another flight attendant to its 737 crews once the number of seats on the planes goes over the current 150. (The FAA requires at least one flight attendant per 50 seats.) 美国人声称：乘客将从这一改变中受益，因为按照联邦航空管理局（FAA）的规定，如果飞机上座椅的数量超过目前的150个座位，他们将在737机组人员中新增一名乘务员。（联邦航空管理局规定一架航班上每50位乘客至少要配备一名乘务员。）（The Economist）② Disconnection between theory and practice is the inevitable attendant of exam-oriented education. 理论与实际脱节是应试教育的必然产物。
[00:39.60]outward a. 表面上的；向外的；外出的；（感情等）外露的 示例 ① It seems that men with traditional views of masculinity are more likely to suppress outward emotions and to fear emotions, supposedly because such feelings may lead to a loss of composure. 对男子气概持传统观念的男性似乎更容易抵制外露的情感，且害怕情感，据说这种感觉会让人难以冷静。（2010. 12）② An outward show of confidence concealed his nervousness. 他表现出很有信心的样子以掩盖内心的紧张。
[00:47.02]scrutiny n. 仔细而彻底的审查 示例 ① England's sweeping laws have been exploited by religious groups, oligarchs and companies objecting to critical or scientific scrutiny. 一直以来，英国大范围的法律都受到反对批判性和科学性调查的各方宗教团体、政治寡头和企业的利用。（The Economist） ② The news media are usually more transparent than businesses because their work product is constantly available for public scrutiny. 新闻媒体通常比企业更透明，因为他们的工作成果要不断地受到公众的审查。
[01:00.42]beneath prep. 在…下面，在…下方；（对某人来说）不够好 示例 ① Described as "electronically controlled flight" by the North American Maglev Transport Institute, the system pushes maglev trains along a magnetic field powered by electricity surging through a guideway a few centimetres beneath them. 这一技术（磁悬浮）被北美磁悬浮运输研究所称为“电子控制的飞机”， 它可以利用磁场推进列车，而磁场所用的电力产生于轨道下方几厘米处的导轨。（The Economist）② Across the world, forests and the soil beneath them absorb about one third of all carbon emissions. 森林与它们下面的土壤能吸收大约全球三分之一的碳排放量。
[01:12.53]controversy n. （公开的）争论，辩论，论战 示例 ① It is these commercial provisions that are proving the settlement's most controversial aspect. 正是这些商业条款证明是该调解方案最具争议性的方面。（2011. 12） ② Controversy indeed surrounded the proposal to build a nuclear power station from the beginning, but this was not a decision taken on a whim. 关于兴建核电站这一提议的争议的确从一开始就存在，但这个提议并不是一时兴起而做的决定。
[01:24.88]discriminate v. 辨别；区别对待，歧视 示例 ① Even now, Hungary and Romania feel peer pressure and face sanctions from their EU partners when they engage in dubious electoral practices, compromise their courts' independence, or discriminate against minorities. 即使是现在，匈牙利和罗马尼亚仍然感受着来自同伴国家的压力，并在选举出现可疑问题、法院的独立性出现妥协或国内的少数民族遭到歧视时，面临来自欧盟伙伴的制裁。（The Guardian）② Russian speakers, who make an extra distinction between light and dark blues in their language, are better able to visually discriminate shades of blue. 俄语对深蓝和浅蓝做了特别细致的区分，所以讲俄语的人能更好地从视觉上辨别蓝色的深浅。
[01:39.21]intent a. 热切的；专注的；坚决的‖n. 意图， 意向，目的 示例 ① Testing drugs in this way—to find out if they can stop a disease from starting—is an ethical minefield because it means experimenting on people who are, to all intents and purposes, healthy. 试验一种药物能否从源头上遏制一种疾病的发生是一个道德雷区，因为这意味着要在几乎完全健康的人身上做实验。（The Economist）② He behaved foolishly but with good intent. 他表现得很愚蠢，但是本意是好的。
[01:47.42]outcome n. 结果，效果 示例 ① The researchers concluded that role model selection can have a positive or negative outcome on a teenager's psychosocial development. 研究人员得出的结论是，榜样的选择能够对青少年社会心理的发展产生正面或者负面的影响。（2013. 6）② It is yet premature to predict the possible outcome of the match. 预言这场比赛的结果还为时尚早。
[01:55.71]enhance v. 提高，增强，增进 示例 ① By some studies, selective schools do enhance their graduates' lifetime earnings.一些研究表明，精英学校的确能够提高其毕业生的终生所得。（2008. 6）② The elegant white wedding dress enhanced her figure and beauty. 优雅的白色婚纱衬托出她曼妙的身材和美丽的容貌。
[02:02.46]paradox n. 矛盾的人（或事物、情况）；悖论 示例 ① It also predicts time is skewed by velocity differences between observers, giving rise to the so-called twin paradox. A twin who returns from a journey in a fast-moving spacecraft will have aged much less than the twin who stayed home. 它（相对论）还预言，时间会因观察者之间的速度差异而被歪曲，它引起了所谓的双生子佯谬：双胞胎中的一个乘坐快速的宇宙飞船完成旅行返回地球时，他的年龄要比留在家里的另一个双胞胎小很多。（New Scientist）② It is a curious paradox that professional comedians are often introverted persons. 职业喜剧演员往往是内向的人，这是个奇怪的矛盾现象。
[02:13.37]instinct n. 本能，天性；直觉 示例 ① But for the survival instinct which nearly all creatures have, more species might have gone extinct on the earth. 若不是因为几乎所有生物都具有的生存本能，更多的物种可能已经在地球上灭绝了。（2012. 6）② Some detectives seem to have an instinct for knowing where clue is to be found. 有些侦探似乎生来就知道哪里能找到破案线索。
[02:23.56]drought n. 久旱，旱灾 示例 ① As harvest season gets under way, farmers find that drought-stressed crops are susceptible to toxins and contaminants, further reducing yields. 收获的季节已经开始，农民发现饱受干旱之苦的农作物易受到毒素和污染的影响，使其产量进一步下降。（Scientific American） ② Long-term solutions are needed to be put forward to save farmers, many of whom have lost most or all of their crops to drought. 必须提出长期的解决方法来拯救农民，他们中的许多人已经因为干旱而失去了大部分或所有农作物。
[02:35.29]prospect n. 可能性；前景；成功的机会‖v. 探矿，勘探 示例 ① But the prospect that income inequality will lead to higher taxes on the wealthy doesn't keep plutocrats up at night. They can live with that. 但是，收入不均可能导致对富人收税更重的可能性并不会使这些有钱有势的人夜不能寐。加重征税他们承受得起。（2007. 12）② Travelling alone around the world wasn't a prospect that I found particularly appealing. 独自一人环游世界对我并不是特别有吸引力。
[02:45.41]revenue n. 财政收入，税收收入，收益 示例 ① The new campus schedules might eventually produce less revenue for the institution and longer working hours for faculty members. 新的校园课程安排最终可能会为学校带来更少的收入，让教职员的工作时间更长。（2012. 6）② The taxes on crude oil and natural gas provide a major source of revenue for the government of that country. 针对原油和天然气的税收是该国政府一项重要的收入。
[02:56.03]so-called a. （表示不认同）所谓的；（引出约定俗成的称谓）人称…的，号称…的 示例 ① Since 2003 the small, elite liberal arts school in Brunswick, Maine, has boosted the proportion of so-called under-represented minority students in entering freshman classes from 8% to 13%. 自2003年以来，这所位于缅因州布伦瑞克市的小型精英文科学校，将所谓的弱势少数民族学生占新生入学人数的比例从8%提高到了13%。（2011. 6）② The so-called panacea was nothing but a scheme to swindle the customers. 所谓的“灵丹妙药” 不过是一个欺骗消费者的骗局。
[03:07.02]reinforce v. 加强；加固；给…加强力量 示例 ① Reinforcement occurs when we receive direct or indirect rewards or punishments for particular gender role behaviours. 强化现象发生在当我们因为做出某些特定的性别角色行为而直接或间接地受到奖励或惩罚之时。（2013. 6）② The climate of political confusion has only reinforced the country's social unrest. 政局混乱只是加剧了该国社会的动荡。
[03:17.86]commercial a. 贸易的，商业的；以获利为目的的 示例 ① So what can be done to create more effective managers of the commercial world? 那么为了打造商界更高效的管理者，我们能做点什么呢？（2011. 6）② Schools should say no to those who donate solely for commercial publicity, because it may affect its independence. 学校应拒绝只是出于商业宣传目的的捐赠， 因为这可能会影响其独立性。
[03:29.38]tolerance n. 宽容，容忍；忍耐（力） 示例 ① Indonesia's main strength in fighting extremism, however, has been its own tradition of moderation and tolerance. 然而，印尼打击极端主义的主要力量一直都是靠本国温和及宽容的传统。（The Economist） ② You must respect the rights of minorities and participate with a spirit of tolerance and compromise. 你必须尊重少数群体的权利， 并怀着宽容与谅解的态度参与其中。
[03:40.74]scheme n. 计划，方案；计谋‖v. 图谋 示例 ① Goodman hopes the scheme will enable active students to fill in any gaps in their experience and encourage their less-active peers to take up activities outside their academic area of work. 古德曼希望该计划能够使活跃的学生填补他们的经验空白，并鼓励他们不太活跃的同学参加学业以外的活动。（2001. 6）② As his own scheme met with little support, the supervisor faced round and supported the ideas of his colleagues. 因为自己的方案几乎没有得到支持，那位主管转而开始赞同同事们的意见。
[03:51.83]grab v. 抓住‖n. 猛然的抓取 示例 ① Leaving it to the Russians to save Cyprus, by letting them recapitalise its banks and grab a slice of its gas, is an answer, but not the best one. 把拯救塞浦路斯留给俄罗斯人，让俄罗斯人对塞浦路斯银行进行资本调整，攫取其一部分天然气， 这是一个解决方法，却不是最好的。（The Economist） ② The two firms also are using each other's distribution networks to grab a larger slice of the market. 两家公司也正在使用对方的销售网络以获取更大的市场份额。
[04:02.44]recession n. 经济衰退；退后，撤回 示例 ① The recession has certainly come with more problems than Andrea anticipated, but she remains unfailingly optimistic. 经济衰退无疑带来了更多的问题，超出了安德烈娅的预料，但是她仍保持无限的乐观。（2012. 12）② Evidence suggests that the global recession has resulted in significant setbacks in the employment levels. 有证据表明，全球范围内的经济衰退已经引起了就业率的大幅下降。
[04:12.16]enormous a. 巨大的，庞大的，极大的 示例 ① What makes going to space the most expensive vacation is the enormous cost involved in the fuel. 使去太空成为最昂贵的旅行的是巨大的燃料成本。（2006. 12）② The massacre of thousands of Jews represents a humanitarian catastrophe of enormous proportions. 屠杀成千上万犹太人是巨大的人道主义灾难。
[04:23.09]solitude n. 独处，独居；孤单 示例 ① The solitude of this peripatetic childhood turned the boy into a writer: he began to publish his stories when he was 11, and never stopped until the day he died. 孤独辗转的童年把这个男孩变成了一位作家：他从11岁就开始出版自己写的故事了， 一直到辞世才停止。（The Economist）② She is searching for a place where she can live in solitude. 她正在寻找一个可以隐居的地方。
[04:32.29]blunder n.（愚蠢或粗心的）错误‖v. 犯（愚蠢的或粗心的）错误 示例 ① For months Obama advisers have argued that his big first-term blunder was trying to reason with congressional Republicans behind closed doors. 几个月以来，奥巴马的顾问们一直认为，奥巴马第一任期内的最大失误就是试图通过与国会共和党议员们的私下会议来说服对方。（The Economist）② It was a serious blunder for them to make compromise and concession on major issue. 他们在重要问题上做出了妥协和让步，那是严重的错误。
[04:41.00]profound a. 深的；深远的；知识渊博的，见解深刻的；极大的 示例 ① They have found that music lessons can produce profound and lasting changes that enhance the general ability to learn. 他们发现，音乐课可以产生深刻而持续的改变，这些改变会提升你的基本学习能力。（2012. 6） ② A learner of profound learning never parades his knowledge. 知识渊博者从不卖弄学问。
[04:48.06]tempt v. 引诱；怂恿 示例 ① It might be tempting, therefore, to think that the old barriers have been broken down and equal opportunity achieved. 因此，这可能会让人觉得过去的传统障碍已经被打破，人人机会均等得到了实现。（2011. 6）② The fineness of the skies tempted her to have a picnic with her friends. 晴朗的天空使她很想和朋友去野餐。
[04:56.79]skilful a. 技术好的，熟练的；制作精良的 示例 ① The reason for England's under-achievement is that it lacks the grassroots infrastructure to develop skilful young players. 英国足球表现不佳的原因在于它缺乏培养球技精湛的年轻球员的机制。（The Economist） ② A teacher who is skilful in delivering his lecture would undoubtedly inspire the mind of his students. 一个有授课技巧的老师毫无疑问能够激发学生的灵感。
[05:07.32]defect n. 缺点，缺陷，毛病‖v. 背叛，叛变， 投敌 示例 ① Whether this actually is a cause of autism is, as yet, unproven. But it is telling that many autistic people have a genetic defect which interferes with their sulphur metabolism. 这是否是造成自闭症的原因还未经证明。但是，有说法称许多患有自闭症的人都存在扰乱硫代谢的基因缺陷。（The Economist）② The merits of your design overweigh the defects. 你的设计中优点大于缺点。
[05:18.04]intensify v. (使)加强，增强，加剧 示例 ① Worries about the effect of libraries on the book trade are not new, but digital devices, which allow books to reach readers with ease and speed, intensify them. 对于图书馆对图书产业影响的忧虑早已不是新鲜事了，但能让读者更加轻松、快捷地获取书籍的电子设备却加剧了这种忧虑。（The Economist） ② WHO calls on all its member states to intensify action against cancer by developing and reinforcing cancer control programmes. 世界卫生组织呼吁其所有成员国通过制定和加强癌症控制规划从而强化防癌行动。
[05:30.32]maintain v. 维持；维修 示例 ① In other words, if middle-class Americans continue to struggle financially as the ultrawealthy grow ever wealthier, it will be increasingly difficult to maintain political support for the free flow of goods, services, and capital across borders. 换言之，如果美国中产阶级继续在经济困境中挣扎，而富豪们更加富裕的话， 要想维持中产阶级对允许商品、服务以及资本自由跨国流通政策的支持将会越来越困难。（2007. 12）② A clothing brand has to tread the tricky path between maintaining good design and keeping prices down. 服装品牌必须在保证良好设计和降低价格间艰难地寻求一条道路。
[05:41.34]obstacle n. 障碍，阻碍；障碍物 示例 ① And when the United States places obstacles in the way of foreign investors and foreign goods, it's likely to encourage reciprocal action abroad. 一旦美国对外国投资者及外国商品设置障碍，很可能会引发别国采取相应行动。（2007. 12） ② His competitor attempted to throw obstacles in the way of his promotion. 他的竞争对手企图阻碍他升职。
[05:50.08]furnish v. 布置家具；供应，提供 示例 ① If these tests are successful, liquid armour could furnish soldiers with protective clothing that is more comfortable and less cumbersome than existing body armour, and provides them with greater protection. 如果测试成功，液体盔甲可以为士兵们提供比现用防弹衣更加舒适、轻便且具有更强防护性能的防护服。（The Economist） ② The ocean waves would furnish human beings with power in the future. 海浪在未来会为人类提供能源。
[05:58.02]launch v. 开始从事；发行；发射‖n. 发射 示例 ① Usually it is left to employers to deduce the potential from a list of extracurricular adventures on a graduate's resume, but now the University of Bristol has launched an award to formalise the achievements of students who devote time to activities outside their courses. 通常是由雇主们根据毕业生简历中所列举的一系列课外冒险活动来推断他的潜质，但现在布里斯托大学正式启动了一个奖项，用于奖励那些利用课余时间参加活动而有所成就的学生。（2011. 6）② The company launched a big advertising campaign to promote their new product. 那家公司发起了一场声势浩大的广告宣传活动以推销他们的新产品。
[06:06.50]exceptional a. 杰出的，优秀的；异常的，罕见的 示例 ① Exceptional efforts will gain an Outstanding Achievement Award. 超常的努力或成就将获得“杰出成就奖”。（2011. 6） ② He showed exceptional talent as a sportsman at the age of six. 他在六岁时就展示出了非凡的体育天赋。
[06:15.59]mechanism n. 机械装置；方法 示例 ① This fear mechanism is critical to the survival of all animals, but no one can say for sure whether beasts other than humans know they're afraid. 恐惧机制对所有动物的生存都是至关重要的，但是没有人敢肯定地说除了人以外，其他动物是否感受到了恐惧。（2006. 12）② The bones and muscles are parts of the mechanism of the body. 骨骼和肌肉是身体结构的组成部分。
[06:21.36]mission n. 使命；代表团；特殊任务‖v. 作艰苦的长途旅行 示例 ① Its overall mission, after all, is to "organise the world's information", so it would be odd if that information did not include books. 它（谷歌）的终极使命毕竟是为了管理世界信息，所以若是这些信息没有将图书涵盖进去就会很奇怪。（2011. 12） ② They have the determination to overcome all the obstacles placed in their path and complete the mission on time. 他们有决心克服道路上的一切障碍并按时完成任务。
[06:31.88]worthy a. 值得…的；值得尊敬的；有价值的 示例 ① Your diligence is worthy of encouragement, but effort does not equal accomplishment.你的勤奋值得鼓励，但努力并不等于成功。（2010. 6） ② He is worthy of the honor for his significant contribution to the mankind's progress of civilisation. 他为人类文明进步做出的巨大贡献配得上这份荣誉。
[06:41.67]confirm v. （提供证据来）证实；使确信；批准 （职位、协议等） 示例 ① The latest research further confirms that the danger lies less in what a motorist's hands do when he takes a call than in what the conversation does to his brain. 最新的研究进一步表明，开车打电话时，对话本身对驾驶者大脑的影响比驾驶者手持电话危险得多。（2009. 12） ② The popular actress refused either to confirm or deny the rumours. 那位当红女演员对流言不置可否。
[06:50.36]initiative n. 新方案；主动性 示例 ① In September the U.S. House of Representatives approved the delightfully named No Child Left Inside Act to encourage public initiatives aimed at exposing kids to the outdoors. 九月份，美国众议院批准了一项名字听起来让人很开心的法案——《不让一个孩子留在室内》，以鼓励孩子们多到室外活动。（2010. 6）② The young man handled all matters strictly by the book, showing little initiative. 那个年轻人办事墨守成规，缺乏创新精神。
